 "result": "The serialization is done by the module-level `_default()` function at `src/tessel/json/provider.py:108`. `StandardJSONProvider` (line 124) installs it as `default = staticmethod(_default)` (line 138), and `json.dumps` calls it for any type it can't serialize natively.\n\n- **Dates:** any `date`, which includes `datetime`, becomes `http_date(o)`, an RFC 822 string.\n- **UUIDs:** `uuid.UUID` becomes `str(o)`. `decimal.Decimal` is handled the same way.\n- **Dataclasses:** an instance becomes `dataclasses.asdict(o)`, which `json.dumps` then serialises as a dict.\n\nAfter those, `_default` has two more cases:\n- Objects with an `__html__` method (such as `Markup`) become `str(o.__html__())`.\n- Anything else raises `TypeError`.\n\nI called the default provider `DefaultJSONProvider` in my last answer, which was wrong. In this repo it's `StandardJSONProvider`, and the `response()` method I described at `provider.py:189` belongs to it.",
